{
  "segments": {
    "topic_intro": {
      "status": "SKIPPED_NOT_SELECTED",
      "reason": "--only-segmentsに含まれないため生成しません",
      "canonical_text": "Today's topic is Package Redelivery: Different Voices."
    },
    "preview": {
      "status": "SKIPPED_NOT_SELECTED",
      "reason": "--only-segmentsに含まれないため生成しません",
      "canonical_text": "A missed package can affect more than the person waiting for it. In this episode, we look at the delivery process and what needs to be considered when trying to reduce missed deliveries."
    },
    "comment_1": {
      "status": "SKIPPED_NOT_SELECTED",
      "reason": "--only-segmentsに含まれないため生成しません",
      "canonical_text": "Listen for what the three people think about charging for another delivery."
    },
    "comment_3": {
      "status": "SKIPPED_NOT_SELECTED",
      "reason": "--only-segmentsに含まれないため生成しません",
      "canonical_text": "Why does the same issue look so different to each person? As you listen to the final thoughts, think about what each person can choose and what feels fair to them."
    },
    "y_lead": {
      "status": "SKIPPED_NOT_SELECTED",
      "reason": "--only-segmentsに含まれないため生成しません",
      "canonical_text": "What if it cost money to have a package delivered again when you were not home at the time it arrived? Charging for redelivery means the person receiving the package pays a fee on top of the usual shipping cost. How should we decide whether to charge a fee or reduce redeliveries in another way? Let’s hear from three people with different lives and points of view.",
